<title>ISRAEL: Palestinian Authority appoints attorney-general.</title>
<headline>Palestinian Authority appoints attorney-general.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1997-07-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Palestinian Authority has appointed a new attorney-general to replace Khaled al-Qidra, who resigned last month.</p>
<p>The attorney-general's office said in a statement that Fayez Abu-Rahmeh, former chairman of the Gaza lawyers' association, took up the post on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;Today is his first day of work,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>Qidra announced last month he was quitting for health reasons.</p>
</text>
